{"archetypes":[{"name":"aggregator-robustness","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new aggregate-findings.sh sits in a non-fatal hot path between collection and voting; partial failure modes, resource cleanup, and fallback correctness are the main risk surface.","prompt_body":"Examine aggregate-findings.sh for incomplete failure recovery: cases where the script exits non-zero despite claiming non-fatal semantics, temp files written but not cleaned up, or the findings.md file left in a partially-overwritten state (e.g. awk write interrupted mid-line). Check whether the `set -euo pipefail` header plus the `set +e` / `set -e` guard around dispatch-with-waterfall is sufficient to prevent early exit from swallowing the non-fatal path. Verify the `awk 1` findings.md overwrite is atomic enough (i.e. reads from a different source than the file it overwrites) and that validation-failure still preserves the original findings.md byte-for-byte. Also check whether the Python validator script written to a tmpdir is cleaned up by the trap. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"schema-migration","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The reviewer field was renamed from a string to a reviewer_slots array and schema_version bumped; downstream consumers (tally-code-votes scoreboard split, compose-review-findings JSONL, lib-vote-tally regex) each touch the attribution format and correctness depends on consistent handling of comma-separated labels across all three sites.","prompt_body":"Trace the full attribution pipeline from reviewer_for_block in lib-vote-tally.sh through the comma-split in tally-code-votes.sh around the score_rows printf, and on to the reviewer_slots JSON array construction in compose-review-findings.sh. Check for off-by-one or whitespace trimming divergences between the awk comma-split in tally-code-votes.sh and the jq split+map in compose-review-findings.sh — specifically whether a trailing space after the last slot or a slot that is only whitespace is handled identically. Verify that the `**Reviewer(s)**:` regex in lib-vote-tally.sh correctly escapes the parentheses for awk (literal `\(s\)` vs regex meta-characters). Check whether the legacy `[Code Review] <Reviewer>` header path in compose-review-findings.sh also emits schema_version and reviewer_slots, or only the body-attribution path does. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sort-removal-impact","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Removing sort -u from collect-findings.sh changes ballot deduplication semantics; the LLM aggregator is the intended replacement but it is non-fatal and can be disabled — understanding the contract boundary between these two mechanisms is important.","prompt_body":"Investigate what `sort -u` was doing in collect-findings.sh before the patch: was it deduplicating exact-duplicate TSV rows produced by multiple reviewer outputs containing identical findings, or was it a side-effect of alphabetical ordering relied on elsewhere? Check whether the downstream `tally-code-votes.sh` loop or `dispatch-code-voters.sh` has any assumption about the ordering or uniqueness of findings.md rows. Examine whether `LARCH_AGGREGATOR_DISABLED=1` (which skips aggregation but keeps the `cp` instead of `sort -u`) could now allow duplicate FINDING_N ids in the ballot file, and whether the voter or tally scripts handle duplicate block ids gracefully. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
